  "example_summary": "Computation of tax liability for Mr. X with a total income of ₹ 16,00,000 for A.Y. 2026-27 under the default tax regime u/s 115BAC.",
  "source_provision": "### Statutory Matrix: Section 115BAC Default Tax Regime\n\n| Total Income Slab | Applicable Tax Rate |\n| :--- | :--- |\n| **Up to ₹ 4,00,000** | NIL |\n| **₹ 4,00,001 – ₹ 8,00,000** | 5% |\n| **₹ 8,00,001 – ₹ 12,00,000** | 10% |\n| **₹ 12,00,001 – ₹ 16,00,000** | 15% |\n| **₹ 16,00,001 – ₹ 20,00,000** | 20% |\n| **₹ 20,00,001 – ₹ 24,00,000** | 25% |\n| **Above ₹ 24,00,000** | 30% |\n\n\n### Key Statutory Rules & Mechanics\n\n* **Default Regime Applicability**: Applies automatically to Individuals, HUFs, AOPs, BOIs, and AJPs unless opted out.\n\n* **Health and Education Cess**: A mandatory **4% Cess** is added to the total Income Tax computed across all progressive slabs.\n\n\n> [!IMPORTANT] Marginal Relief & Rebate: Assessees under the default tax regime u/s 115BAC are eligible for Rebate u/s 87A subject to specified statutory threshold limits for the relevant Assessment Year.",
